<p>"Editorial minimal" KPI indicator. <strong>Magazine-cover restraint</strong> — six KPIs in a 2×3 grid, hairline rules between cells, light-weight numerals, no charts, no pills, no decorations. The whole design's expressive energy goes into <em>one</em> thing: a generous, low-weight number that owns the cell. The label is a tiny uppercase mono caption above it; the delta and target sit beneath as a small meta row. Built for executive dashboards / weekly review pages where the operator wants to see "how are we doing" at a glance and read the supporting context only on hover. Renders as a <strong>table card</strong> (zero card-body padding, dividers go edge-to-edge to the card border).</p>

<style>
/* === Card chrome === */
.kpi-edit__header {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 1.6rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}
.kpi-edit__live {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  color: var(--pa-text-secondary);
}
.kpi-edit__livedot {
  width: 0.8rem;
  height: 0.8rem;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--pa-positive);
  box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--pa-positive);
  animation: kpiPulse 1.6s ease-in-out infinite;
}
@keyframes kpiPulse { 50% { opacity: 0.35; } }

/* Table-card mode: zero card-body padding so the hairline rules go
   edge-to-edge. Each tile carries its own padding, and the 1px
   gap-as-divider trick (below) handles the inter-tile rules. */
.kpi-edit__body { padding: 0; }

/* === Grid + hairline rules ===
   Using `gap: 1px` over `background: var(--pa-border-color)` with each
   tile painting `background: var(--pa-card-bg)` on top — this paints
   single-pixel hairlines on every interior boundary (vertical *and*
   horizontal) for free, without per-cell border bookkeeping or
   double-border seams. The card's outer border supplies the perimeter
   so the rules stop cleanly at the card edge.

   Container query (not media query) so the 3-col layout adapts based on
   the *card's* width, not the viewport — so the same markup collapses
   to 2-col at 1×3 page-grid widths and 1-col inside narrow 25% cells,
   while the canonical full-width card stays 3-col. */
.kpi-edit__grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  gap: 1px;
  background: var(--pa-border-color);
  container-type: inline-size;
}
@container (max-width: 640px) {
  .kpi-edit__grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
}
@container (max-width: 360px) {
  .kpi-edit__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}

/* Modifier: force 2-col regardless of card width. For placements
   where the host wants a deterministic 2×N layout (e.g. 4 tiles
   shown as a clean 2×2) instead of relying on the container query
   to land in the right bucket — viewport width varies enough that
   "1/3 of the page" can be 400px or 800px depending on monitor
   size, and a forced 2-col removes that ambiguity. Placed after
   the container queries so it wins by source order. */
.kpi-edit__grid--2col { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }

/* Tile — generous padding (2.4rem) is the "editorial space" the design
   leans on. Background paints over the grid's border-color background
   to leave only 1px showing as the hairline. */
.kpi-edit__tile {
  background: var(--pa-card-bg);
  padding: 2.4rem 2rem;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 1.2rem;
  position: relative;
  min-width: 0; /* allow long values to wrap rather than overflow the column */
}

/* Label — uppercase mono, two-line allowance for "MONTHLY REVENUE" /
   "SERVER CAPACITY". Low contrast so it stays a caption, not a heading. */
.kpi-edit__label {
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 50%, transparent);
  line-height: 1.3;
}

/* Value — the editorial signature.
   - NOT mono. Mono fonts rarely have a true 200 weight; using the body
     sans gives us proper thin glyphs that read as "editorial" rather
     than "monospace at low contrast".
   - font-weight: 200 (extra-light). 300 was tested first but didn't
     read distinctly enough as "light" against the body's 400 default.
   - clamp() lets the number shrink in narrow page-grid cells (25%
     column) without manual breakpoints. Capped at 5.6rem so it doesn't
     get absurd at very wide canonical widths. */
.kpi-edit__value {
  font-family: var(--base-font-family);
  font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 18cqi, 5.6rem);
  font-weight: 200;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  line-height: 1;
  color: var(--pa-text-color-1);
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.2rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}
.kpi-edit__num {
  font-weight: 200;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
.kpi-edit__unit {
  font-size: 0.4em;
  font-weight: 300;
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 50%, transparent);
  letter-spacing: 0;
}

/* Meta row — delta + target sit on a single line below the value.
   Mono so the numbers tabulate; small so they read as supporting,
   not as another headline. */
.kpi-edit__meta {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 1.4rem;
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.3rem;
  line-height: 1.3;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}
.kpi-edit__delta {
  font-weight: 700;
  white-space: nowrap;
  color: var(--pa-positive);
}
.kpi-edit__delta--positive    { color: var(--pa-positive); }
.kpi-edit__delta--negative    { color: var(--pa-negative); }
.kpi-edit__delta--neutral     { color: var(--pa-neutral); }
.kpi-edit__delta--up-strong   { color: var(--pa-very-positive); }
.kpi-edit__delta--down-strong { color: var(--pa-very-negative); }
.kpi-edit__target {
  font-weight: 500;
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 50%, transparent);
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.kpi-edit__target em {
  font-style: normal;
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 38%, transparent);
  margin-right: 0.5rem;
}

/* Hover host — a faint wash over the whole tile so the cursor-anchored
   popover has a clear "this tile" anchor. */
.kpi-edit__tile:hover {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 4%, var(--pa-card-bg));
}

/* === Footer caption === */
.kpi-edit__footer {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 1rem;
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: var(--pa-text-secondary);
}
.kpi-edit__footer strong {
  color: var(--pa-text-color-1);
  font-weight: 700;
}

/* === Hover detail popover (cursor-anchored, same recipe as elsewhere) === */
.kpi-edit-detail {
  position: fixed;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  visibility: hidden;
  pointer-events: none;
  z-index: 9000;
  min-width: 24rem;
  max-width: 30rem;
  background: var(--pa-detail-bg);
  color: var(--pa-detail-text);
  padding: 1.1rem 1.4rem;
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  line-height: 1.5;
  border-radius: 0.4rem;
  box-shadow: var(--pa-detail-shadow);
}
.kpi-edit-detail[data-show] { visibility: visible; }
.kpi-edit-detail-title {
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  font-size: 1.05rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--pa-detail-title);
  margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
}
.kpi-edit-detail dl {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
  gap: 0.35rem 1.6rem;
  margin: 0;
}
.kpi-edit-detail dt { margin: 0; color: var(--pa-detail-row-label); font-weight: 400; }
.kpi-edit-detail dd { margin: 0; text-align: end; font-weight: 600; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.kpi-edit-detail .pos { color: var(--pa-positive); }
.kpi-edit-detail .neg { color: var(--pa-negative); }
.kpi-edit-detail .warn { color: var(--pa-warning); }
</style>

